  "discussion": "Due to the use of wear levelling in non-volatile flash memory media, and the potential for bad memory blocks, it is possible that not all memory blocks will be overwritten during sanitisation processes. For this reason, SECRET and TOP SECRET non-volatile flash memory media retains its classification following sanitisation.",
